<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1><i class="fas fa-link"></i> Deep Link Exploitation</h1><div class="lab-info"><span class="lab-tag difficulty-medium">Medium</span></div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2><p>The app registers custom URL schemes without proper validation. Craft malicious deep links that trigger unintended actions like account takeover or data exfiltration.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> Deep Link Tester</h2>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4>Registered URL Schemes (from AndroidManifest.xml):</h4>
        <pre>
&lt;intent-filter&gt;
  &lt;action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW"/&gt;
  &lt;category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT"/&gt;
  &lt;data android:scheme="hacklab"
        android:host="app"
        android:pathPrefix="/"/&gt;
&lt;/intent-filter&gt;

Known paths: /login, /reset-password, /transfer, /admin
        </pre>
      </div>
      <div class="vulnerable-form" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <label for="deepLink">Deep Link URL:</label>
          <input type="text" id="deepLink" placeholder="hacklab://app/reset-password?token=..." value="hacklab://app/login?redirect=">
        </div>
        <button class="btn" onclick="testDeepLink()"><i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Test Deep Link</button>
      </div>
      <div id="deepLinkResults" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> Hints</h4>
        <pre>
# Try exploiting the redirect parameter:
# hacklab://app/login?redirect=https://evil.com
# hacklab://app/transfer?to=attacker&amount=9999
# hacklab://app/admin?token=null

# Deep link injection via web:
# &lt;a href="hacklab://app/reset-password?email=victim@corp.com"&gt;
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flag-submit"><h3><i class="fas fa-flag"></i> Capture The Flag</h3>
      <form onsubmit="submitFlagInline('mobile-deep-links','flagInput_deep','flagResult_deep'); return false;" style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto;"><input type="text" id="flagInput_deep" placeholder="FLAG{...}" autocomplete="off"><button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button></form>
      <div id="flagResult_deep" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>
    async function testDeepLink() {
      const url = document.getElementById('deepLink').value;
      const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('deepLinkResults');
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:var(--primary)"><i class="fas fa-spinner fa-spin"></i> Testing deep link...</p>';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/labs/mobile/deep-links', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify({ url }) });
        const data = await res.json();
        let html = '<h4 style="color:var(--primary)">Deep Link Response:</h4>';
        html += '<pre style="color:var(--text);white-space:pre-wrap;">' + (data.result || data.error || 'No response') + '</pre>';
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = html;
      } catch(e) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#ff4444">Error: ' + e.message + '</p>'; }
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
